id: decisions/034-proof-scope-fidelity
title: "A proof names the claim it covers"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'proof-scope-fidelity'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: proof-scope-fidelity
axis_gloss: "whether the attached proof actually covers the claim it sits under, or covers a narrower or different claim than the one advertised"
poles:
  a: proof-overreach
  b: scope-matched-proof
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 7.6
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(9) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Must every proof block say exactly which claim it covers, so that a passing
  check can never be read as proving the whole record?

why_it_matters: >
  Five written rules scope proof narrowly (a passing proof does not retire
  intent or cost; a receipt proves equivalence, not origin; no cited study tests
  interception as defined), but core/canonical-extension.yawn carries a green
  proof block whose validator checks only the extension name while the same
  record's media_role claim is falsified by two JSON .yawn files nobody checks.
  A bot inherits whether a passing proof on a record means every line is proven;
  a child Yawn learns whether to write proof.covers.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    3 judgments sit at proof-overreach (0 authored) and 6 at scope-matched-proof
    (5 authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave wants the two JSON templates
    (templates/question-proposal.v1.yawn, templates/art-brief.v1.yawn) recognised
    as a second grammar or removed; that decides whether media_role is a claim to
    prove or to drop.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      A proof block sits at the top of a record and stands for the record. A passing
      check makes the record proven.
    cost: "Nothing changes."
    risk: "Every claim in the 128 proof-bearing files inherits the strength of whatever narrow check happens to sit under proof:, which is how media_role reads as proven today (FACT 10)."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None; A is the status quo."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0187"
      - "J0718"
      - "J0727"
  - name: B
    description: >
      Every proof block names the claims it covers under proof.covers: as key paths
      in the same record. Any claim not listed is unproven by default. A checklist's
      checked box counts only for the claim it names.
    cost: "A covers: line in 128 proof blocks, phased through a shrink-only ledger; core/canonical-extension.yawn either adds a media_role check to its validator or lists media_role as uncovered; references/source-index.yawn proof.source matched to its sources; fixtures/node.yawn and schemas/node.yawn agree on the strength of npm test."
    risk: "covers: lines written broadly (covers: all) defeat the rule; needs a lint that covers: names existing keys."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/canonical-extension-v1.test.mjs to assert each acceptance condition in the core/canonical-extension.yawn proof block corresponds to a pattern in scripts/validate-canonical-extension.mjs (today media_role has none); a new test that every proof block with a command or verifier carries covers: naming keys that exist in the same record, with a grandfather map."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0210"
      - "J0328"
      - "J0541"
      - "J0600"
      - "J0688"
      - "J1117"
  - name: C
    description: >
      Option B for every record whose proof names a command, test, verifier or
      validator (the executable layer) and every record with status active or v1.
      Seed-backed source lists are exempt and are lineage, not proof (see the
      what-counts-as-proof decision).
    cost: "covers: on roughly twenty executable proof blocks and the 37 active or v1 files; the same three fixes as B."
    risk: "The exemption leaves the majority of proof blocks unscoped; readers must know the two regimes."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Same tests as B, scoped to records whose proof block names something runnable or whose status is active or v1."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0210"
      - "J0328"
      - "J0600"
      - "J1117"

recommendation:
  option_ref: B
  confidence: 0.75
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Five of six scope-matched judgments are authored, one proof-attached (J0600)
    and one contract-defined (J1117, where the receipt schema writes its limit
    into its own description). The overreach cases are unauthored readings, and
    GROUND_TRUTH FACT 10 finds the sharpest instance in the flagship validator:
    the proof block covers the name and the record wears it over media_role, which
    FACT 9 falsifies. B is the honest rule and its cost is one line per proof
    block, which the grandfather pattern can phase; C is B minus the seed-backed
    majority, which only makes sense if the what-counts-as-proof decision has
    already turned those into lineage.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "core/canonical-extension.yawn proof block lists media_role under covers: with a check in scripts/validate-canonical-extension.mjs, or lists it as uncovered"
    - "references/source-index.yawn proof.source equals its sources list or states why it differs"
    - "fixtures/node.yawn and schemas/node.yawn either claim the same strength for npm test or state the difference"
    - "A test in tests/ asserts every executable proof block carries covers: naming keys that exist in that record, and passes"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A record's proof passes while a claim in the same record is false and no field
    distinguishes the two; media_role in core/canonical-extension.yawn is the live
    instance.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0187"
  - "J0718"
  - "J0727"
  - "J0210"
  - "J0328"
  - "J0541"
  - "J0600"
  - "J0688"
  - "J1117"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
